From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@conda-forge.org>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: cmake: do not make missing-field-initializers fatal

cmake/level-zero.cmake targets Level Zero 1.27.0, but the driver is often
built against whatever Level Zero loader the system provides, so that the
userspace driver matches the loader that dlopens it at runtime. Newer
loader headers add members to the Level Zero DDI tables, for example
ze_command_list_dditable_t::pfnAppendMemoryCopyWithParameters and
ze_device_dditable_t::pfnGetRuntimeRequirements.

The driver fills those tables with designated initializers naming only the
entries it implements, so any newer member is value-initialized to null:

    umd/level_zero_driver/api/ze_cmdlist.cpp:658: error: missing
      initializer for member
      '_ze_command_list_dditable_t::pfnAppendMemoryCopyWithParameters'
      [-Werror=missing-field-initializers]

Leaving those entries null is correct: they are entry points this driver
predates, and the loader treats a null entry as unsupported. Only the
combination with -Werror in cmake/compiler_flags.cmake turns the warning
into a build failure, which makes the driver fail to compile against any
loader newer than the pinned one.

Keep the warning but drop it back to non-fatal, rather than requiring
downstreams to pin an older Level Zero than the one their users run
against.

Signed-off-by: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@conda-forge.org>

---
 cmake/compiler_flags.cmake | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)
diff --git a/cmake/compiler_flags.cmake b/cmake/compiler_flags.cmake
index 0cc74c7..cfd1715 100644
--- a/cmake/compiler_flags.cmake
+++ b/cmake/compiler_flags.cmake
@@ -5,6 +5,12 @@
 add_compile_options(
   # Compiler warnings
   -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Wno-unused-parameter -Wvla -Wno-error=cpp
+  # The Level Zero loader headers we build against (conda-forge
+  # level-zero) are newer than the version this driver targets, so the
+  # DDI tables it fills have members it does not initialize. Those are
+  # intentionally left null (features this driver predates); keep the
+  # warning but do not let -Werror turn it into a hard failure.
+  -Wno-error=missing-field-initializers
   # Control flow integrity
   $<$<CONFIG:Release>:-fcf-protection=full>
   # Format string defence
